f given)", "ref": "Kruger et al. (2017) ch.9 magnitude band 1e-3..1e-2, cited WITHOUT page/table number -> no quantitative error possible; goal demanded original table/page (zero hand-copy)", "reported_by_m15468": {"baseline_bgk_lattice_1500steps": 0.000398142870005413, "bgk_geometric_1500steps": 0.003277983214579357, "3d_edm_n32_400steps": 0.007097419094111377, "converged_2d": false, "converged_3d": false}, "auditor_recomputed_2d": {"repro_rerun_baseline": 0.0003981429, "repro_rerun_geometric": 0.003277983, "repro_bit_identical": true, "converged_plateau_baseline": {"u_max": 0.00017337158650439, "steps": 5400, "converged": true, "pass": true}, "converged_plateau_geometric": {"u_max": 0.003354801835395981, "steps": 4500, "converged": true, "pass": false}, "transient_peak_both": 0.0397}, "auditor_recomputed_3d": {"u_max": 0.13447539947741344, "R_eq": 7.489877008078426, "dp": 0.012851533331687507, "sigma": 0.048128202009779894, "finite": true, "reported_u_max": 0.007097419094111377, "reported_R_eq": 17.358341738695955, "reported_dp": "NaN", "reported_sigma": "NaN", "reported_finite": false, "underestimate_factor": 19.0, "verdict": "3D artifact NOT reproducible from its own declared parameters (R_eq 17.36 > half box 16 is geometrically impossible; dp=NaN because far band r>1.5*R_eq is empty, pseudopotential_edm3d.py:687-712)"}, "verdicts": "2D baseline PASS confirmed (transient 3.98e-4 -> converged plateau 1.73e-4, both <1e-3); 2D geometric FAIL confirmed (3.36e-3); 3D point invalid (unreproducible, dp/sigma NaN, finite=false) and cannot be used as a validation point", "cross_benchmark_divergence": "docs/MCMP_VERIFY_BENCH.md section 2 gives converged |u|max=9.3e-3 for the SAME nominal case (n=96, G_12=-2.5, R=24) vs this case's plateau 1.73e-4 -> 54x, unexplained (different psi/forcing/velocity convention) (F3)", "zero_handcopy_claim_false": "report header claims all numbers programmatically injected, but sections 5.1/5.2 tables are hand-transcribed from docs/MCMP_VERIFY_BENCH.md section 2 (0.0103/0.0097/0.0093; 0.0177/0.0164/0.0157; 0.0257/0.0239/0.0228 all digit-identical)"}, "repro_cmd": "bash audit/repro_mcmp_spurious.sh  # rc=0, ~36 s, reproduces 2D values bit-identically; converged plateau: audit/mcmp_convergence_probe.py <method> <out.json>; 3D: audit/mcmp3d_probe.py (35 s)", "external_anchor": "docs/CASE_MCMP_SPURIOUS_REPORT.md", "external_anchor_note": "cites Kruger et al. (2017) The Lattice Boltzmann Method ch.9 band 1e-3..1e-2 and Connington & Lee (2012) J.Stat.Mech P04001, but with NO page/table number and no single reference value -> not a quantitative external anchor (L5 not met)", "level_rationale": "L2 = real end-to-end function: existing D2Q9/D3Q19 engines produce the diagnostic numbers and the 2D values reproduce bit-identically under an independent audit re-run. NOT L3 (no main-solver/platform caller; anchor unregistered). NOT L4: no benchmark referee row, ref is a magnitude band without page/table so no quantitative error, repro script was never committed and the branch is unmerged, and the 3D point is unreproducible (dp/sigma=NaN, finite=false, R_eq exceeds half-box, u_max understated 19x), plus a 54x unexplained divergence from the repo's own converged benchmark of the same nominal case.", "findings": ["F1 blocking: 3D artifact unreproducible - audit re-run of the declared params gives u_max=1.345e-01, R_eq=7.49, dp=1.285e-02, finite=true vs delivered u_max=7.10e-03, R_eq=17.36, dp/sigma=NaN, finite=false; report section 3.2 presents this as a validation point without flagging NaN/R_eq>half-box (19x understatement)", "F2 blocking: repro_cmd never committed (git ls-files runs/repro_mcmp_spurious.sh = 0) and branch agent/m15468 unmerged into main -> delivered repo cannot reproduce (three-piece rule broken)", "F3 medium: 54x divergence between this case (plateau 1.73e-4) and the repo's own converged benchmark of the same nominal configuration (9.3e-3, MCMP_VERIFY_BENCH.md s.2) left unexplained; literature-band comparison is not like-for-like", "F4 medium: tensor_benchmark_cases has 0 rows for anchor_slug='CASE-MCMP-SPURIOUS' -> no machine referee; 'in tolerance' cannot be adjudicated from the ledger", "F5 low: report claims 'zero hand-copy' but s.5.1/5.2 are transcribed tables (values digit-identical to MCMP_VERIFY_BENCH.md); committed JSON has 7 keys while the repro script writes 4 -> artifact came from an ad-hoc wrapper (provenance gap)", "F6 low: the PASS headline rests on a non-converged 1500-step transient (converged=false) even though convergence improved the result; report should state the plateau value"], "rework_request": "1) single-value ref with page/table; 2) re-deliver 2D numbers at converged plateau (stop_tol<=1e-4, >=5400 steps); 3) fix 3D geometry (R_eq<=0.25N i.e. n>=4R) and assert finite=true & dp>0 else honest-FAIL; 4) commit runs/repro_*.sh with parameter fingerprint (rho_min/rho_max/R0/width); 5) register anchor in tensor_benchmark_cases; 6) explain/remove the 54x divergence vs MCMP_VERIFY_BENCH.md", "not_run": ["full W x G_12 x N sweep (only the minimum set needed for the convergence/referee decision)", "GPU/SDAA backend", "no source change to the audited delivery (verification ticket, not remediation)"]}$json$::jsonb, 'board-audit')
